            "text": "{\"findings\":[{\"tipo\":\"GPU\",\"causa_raiz\":\"O tempo de GPU atingiu 26.38ms (117 violações), ultrapassando severamente o budget de 16.67ms necessário para manter 60 FPS na GTX 1650. Como os Draw Calls (904) estão bem abaixo do teto de 2579, o gargalo reside na taxa de preenchimento (Fillrate/Overdraw), complexidade de fragment shaders, resoluções de renderização nativas sem escala dinâmica ou custo excessivo de pós-processamento/sombras em tempo real.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\nusing UnityEngine.Rendering;\\\\n\\\\npublic class GpuPerformanceOptimizer : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    [Header(\\\"Dynamic Resolution & Frame Target\\\")]\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float targetFrameTimeMs = 16.0f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float minResolutionScale = 0.65f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float maxResolutionScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    \\\\n    private Camera targetCamera;\\\\n    private float currentScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    private const int SampleWindow = 15;\\\\n    private float[] frameTimes = new float[SampleWindow];\\\\n    private int sampleIndex = 0;\\\\n\\\\n    private void Awake()\\\\n    {\\\\n        targetCamera = GetComponent\u003cCamera\u003e();\\\\n        if (targetCamera == null)\\\\n        {\\\\n            targetCamera = Camera.main;\\\\n        }\\\\n        \\\\n        Application.targetFrameRate = 60;\\\\n        QualitySettings.vSyncCount = 1;\\\\n        \\\\n        // Otimizacoes de GPU para hardware legado\\\\n        QualitySettings.shadowDistance = Mathf.Min(QualitySettings.shadowDistance, 45f);\\\\n        QualitySettings.shadowCascades = 2;\\\\n        QualitySettings.shadowResolution = ShadowResolution.Medium;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void Update()\\\\n    {\\\\n        frameTimes[sampleIndex] = Time.unscaledDeltaTime * 1000f;\\\\n        sampleIndex = (sampleIndex + 1) % SampleWindow;\\\\n\\\\n        float avgFrameTime = 0f;\\\\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c SampleWindow; i++)\\\\n        {\\\\n            avgFrameTime += frameTimes[i];\\\\n        }\\\\n        avgFrameTime /= SampleWindow;\\\\n\\\\n        if (avgFrameTime \u003e targetFrameTimeMs)\\\\n        {\\\\n            currentScale = Mathf.Max(minResolutionScale, currentScale - 0.05f * Time.unscaledDeltaTime);\\\\n        }\\\\n        else if (avgFrameTime \u003c targetFrameTimeMs - 3.0f)\\\\n        {\\\\n            currentScale = Mathf.Min(maxResolutionScale, currentScale + 0.05f * Time.unscaledDeltaTime);\\\\n        }\\\\n\\\\n        ScalableBufferManager.ResizeBuffers(currentScale, currentScale);\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"A placa de vídeo (GPU) está demorando quase 27 milissegundos para desenhar a imagem na tela, o que impede o jogo de alcançar os 60 quadros por segundo (que exige no máximo 16.6ms). Como a quantidade de objetos desenhados (draw calls) está segura, o problema é a quantidade de pixels complexos processados por quadro. O script ajusta a resolução interna de renderização e configurações de sombra de forma dinâmica, aliviando a carga da GPU sem mexer no tamanho da janela do jogador.\"},{\"tipo\":\"GC\",\"causa_raiz\":\"Ocorrência de 33.695 bytes alocados no frame monitorado. Alocações frequentes na Heap disparam coletas imprevisíveis do Garbage Collector, gerando micro-engasgos (stuttering).\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\n\\\\npublic class NonAllocBufferExample : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    // Reutilizacao de buffer fixo sem instanciar novos arrays no Update\\\\n    private static readonly RaycastHit[] HitBuffer = new RaycastHit[16];\\\\n    \\\\n    public int CheckSurroundings(Vector3 origin, Vector3 direction, float distance, LayerMask mask)\\\\n    {\\\\n        // Substitui Physics.RaycastAll (que aloca novo array na Heap) pela versao NonAlloc\\\\n        int hitCount = Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(origin, direction, HitBuffer, distance, mask);\\\\n        return hitCount;\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"Quan